                <pb facs="0879" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">484.11 Young, Reuben S., No. 2/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Southard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-31T18:00:00-04:00">August 31, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Your 11, August 25, 4 p.m. Although an offer of two thousand Ethiopian
                    dollars in full settlement of Young’s claim appears to be <pb facs="0880"
                        n="780" xml:id="pg780"/> somewhat incommensurate with the gravity of the
                    offense, you may inform the competent Ethiopian authorities that this Government
                    is prepared to accept the offer provided that payment is made without delay. You
                    may also state that this Government notes with satisfaction that the Ethiopian
                    official responsible for the treaty violation is to be punished.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
